WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.688
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.988 --> 00:00:08.468
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.768 --> 00:00:14.868
Unit fourteen: Managing Money. In this unit, you will talk about budgets, saving and obligations.

4
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:16.838
budget plan.

5
00:00:17.538 --> 00:00:20.664
budget plan means a plan of how you will spend and save your money.

6
00:00:20.964 --> 00:00:23.880
I made a budget plan for my first month at university.

7
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.606
Your turn. Say: budget plan.

8
00:00:29.306 --> 00:00:30.342
budget plan.

9
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.084
debt.

10
00:00:32.784 --> 00:00:34.586
debt means money that you owe someone.

11
00:00:34.886 --> 00:00:37.002
He worked two jobs to pay off his debt.

12
00:00:37.702 --> 00:00:40.110
Your turn. Say: debt.

13
00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.521
debt.

14
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:45.553
credit card.

15
00:00:46.253 --> 00:00:49.158
credit card means a card that lets you buy now and pay later.

16
00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:52.340
Be careful: a credit card can make you overspend.

17
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.146
Your turn. Say: credit card.

18
00:00:57.846 --> 00:00:58.929
credit card.

19
00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:00.929
interest rate.

20
00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:04.871
interest rate means the percentage you pay extra when you borrow money.

21
00:01:05.171 --> 00:01:07.589
The bank's interest rate is seven percent a year.

22
00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:10.987
Your turn. Say: interest rate.

23
00:01:13.687 --> 00:01:14.828
interest rate.

24
00:01:15.817 --> 00:01:17.062
emergency fund.

25
00:01:17.762 --> 00:01:21.317
emergency fund means money saved for unexpected problems.

26
00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:25.671
Experts say an emergency fund should cover three months of costs.

27
00:01:26.371 --> 00:01:29.163
Your turn. Say: emergency fund.

28
00:01:31.863 --> 00:01:33.224
emergency fund.

29
00:01:34.217 --> 00:01:35.206
monthly bill.

30
00:01:35.906 --> 00:01:38.753
monthly bill means a payment you must make every month.

31
00:01:39.053 --> 00:01:41.180
Our biggest monthly bill is the rent.

32
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.976
Your turn. Say: monthly bill.

33
00:01:46.676 --> 00:01:47.665
monthly bill.

34
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.023
financial advice.

35
00:01:50.723 --> 00:01:53.628
financial advice means help from an expert about money.

36
00:01:53.928 --> 00:01:56.241
She asked her bank for financial advice.

37
00:01:56.941 --> 00:01:59.628
Your turn. Say: financial advice.

38
00:02:02.328 --> 00:02:03.851
financial advice.

39
00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:05.851
invest.

40
00:02:06.551 --> 00:02:09.491
invest means to put money into something to make more money.

41
00:02:09.791 --> 00:02:12.487
Many young people invest in small businesses.

42
00:02:13.187 --> 00:02:15.410
Your turn. Say: invest.

43
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.181
invest.

44
00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:22.229
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:22.529 --> 00:02:25.934
I got my first salary, but it's almost gone!

46
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.599
Do you have a budget plan? You have to know where your money goes.

47
00:02:31.883 --> 00:02:35.418
Not yet. I must pay my monthly bills first, right?

48
00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:39.624
Yes. And you should start an emergency fund.

49
00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:42.638
Do I have to get a credit card?

50
00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:48.274
No, you don't have to. Be careful: the interest rate can be very high.

51
00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:52.268
Grammar focus: must · have to · don't have to.

52
00:02:52.568 --> 00:02:55.206
Use must or have to when something is necessary.

53
00:02:55.506 --> 00:02:59.633
Mustn't means it is not allowed. Don't have to means it is not necessary.

54
00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:04.010
For example: You mustn't share your PIN, but you don't have to pay in cash.

55
00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:08.493
Mustn't and don't have to have very different meanings: one is forbidden, the other is optional.

56
00:03:09.483 --> 00:03:13.227
Now read and listen. The 50-30-20 Rule.

57
00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:19.219
Many financial experts recommend a simple budget plan called the 50-30-20 rule.

58
00:03:20.517 --> 00:03:24.362
Fifty percent of your income goes to needs, like rent and monthly bills.

59
00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:28.834
Thirty percent is for wants, such as eating out and hobbies.

60
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:35.075
The last twenty percent must go to savings, an emergency fund or paying off debt.

61
00:03:36.383 --> 00:03:40.240
You don't have to follow it exactly, but it is a great place to start.

62
00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.121
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:44.421 --> 00:03:46.455
Money that you owe someone is blank.

64
00:03:46.755 --> 00:03:50.049
A, debt. B, invest. C, budget plan.

65
00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.864
The answer is A: debt.

66
00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:00.397
You blank wear a seatbelt in a car. It's the law.

67
00:04:00.697 --> 00:04:03.561
A, don't have to. B, must. C, mustn't.

68
00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.236
The answer is B: must.

69
00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.342
It's a holiday tomorrow, so we blank go to work.

70
00:04:13.642 --> 00:04:17.086
A, mustn't. B, don't have to. C, must.

71
00:04:21.083 --> 00:04:23.002
The answer is B: don't have to.

72
00:04:24.517 --> 00:04:27.282
Money saved for unexpected problems is an blank.

73
00:04:27.582 --> 00:04:31.747
A, interest rate. B, emergency fund. C, credit card.

74
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.318
The answer is B: emergency fund.

75
00:04:39.817 --> 00:04:42.699
According to the text, what percentage goes to savings?

76
00:04:42.999 --> 00:04:46.873
A, fifty percent. B, thirty percent. C, twenty percent.

77
00:04:50.883 --> 00:04:53.115
The answer is C: twenty percent.

78
00:04:54.617 --> 00:04:57.942
Now it's your turn to speak. What are your tips for saving money?

79
00:05:03.242 --> 00:05:08.528
I have to pay my bills first, then I save twenty percent, and I don't buy things I don't need.

80
00:05:08.828 --> 00:05:10.490
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:11.483 --> 00:05:15.355
Great work today! You learned eight new words and must · have to · don't have to.

82
00:05:15.655 --> 00:05:19.387
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

83
00:05:19.687 --> 00:05:22.246
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:22.546 --> 00:05:25.373
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

